Secuirty Headers

1.add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000";
    security header that forces browsers to use HTTPS only for your site
    
    (support HSTS http strict transport Secuirty)

    Without HSTS:
        A user might first hit http://yourdomain.com 
        An attacker can intercept (MITM attack)

2. add_header X-Frame-Options DENY; prevent server from iframe content
                X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
                X-Frame-Options "ALLOW-FROM https://yourdomain.com"

3. add_header X-Content-Type-Options "no sniff" always;
    Browser may treat a .txt file as JS → security risk
    Tells browser:
        “Use only the declared Content-Type”
        Don’t try to guess
                
4. add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    block Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

5. add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always; recommends

    add_header Referrer-Policy ->how much referrer URL info is sent when users click links.
     
    unsafe-url -> Sends full URL everywhere

    no-referrer -> No referrer sent ever

    no-referrer-when-downgrade -> Send referrer only HTTPS → HTTPS

    origin -> send only domain
    origin-when-cross-origin -> Same origin → full URL
                              Cross origin → only domain
    same-origin -> Send only for same site
    strict-origin -> Send origin only on secure requests
    strict-origin-when-cross-origin -> Same origin → full URL domain.com/index.html
                                        Cross origin → only origin domain.com
                                        HTTPS → HTTP → ❌ no referrer


6. add_header  Content-Security-Policy -> HTTP response header that controls what resources a browser is allowed to 
                                        load (scripts, styles, images, frames, etc.). 
                                        It’s your strongest defense against XSS, data injection, and clickjacking.

default-src 'self'; Applies to all resource types if not specified
script-src 'self' https://cdn.example.com; Controls JavaScript sources
    'self' → same domain
    'none' → block all
style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com;
img-src 'self' data: allows base64 images
form-action 'self';
frame-ancestors 'self' ; Replaces X-Frame-Options
upgrade-insecure-requests; Converts HTTP → HTTPS automatically
add connect-src 'self' https://api.unemployengineer.works;
    controls where your frontend is allowed to make network requests.

